{"seq":2,"time":1789095363332,"type":"request/header","data":{"reason":"initial","system":"Role: Coordinator.","tools":[{"name":"wait","description":"Wait until every task added to this episode's board has settled and no child reservation remains. Their reports are in the request that follows. Returns at once when the board has no added task. Use it before acting on delegated work. An episode that ends while a child runs ends that child. With `until`, wait instead until an arrival matches one condition. That form states how long it will block: name `timeout_seconds` unless this episode has a seconds budget. The result names the condition met, or `timeout`. The arrival itself is in the request that follows.","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"timeout_seconds":{"description":"return after this long even if nothing matched","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"until":{"description":"conditions, of which the first met ends the wait: {child, outcome?} for a child episode (id, or \"any\") reaching any outcome or the named kind; {session} for a process session (id, or \"any\") exiting; {inbox} for an inbox arrival by source; {reply} for the answer to the question whose message_id `ask` returned","items":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"child":{"description":"child episode id, or \"any\"","type":"string"},"outcome":{"enum":["completed","blocked","exhausted","failed"],"type":"string"}},"required":["child"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"session":{"description":"session id, or \"any\"","type":["integer","string"]}},"required":["session"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"inbox":{"enum":["task","parent","child","peer","request","response","verify","system","session"],"type":"string"}},"required":["inbox"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"reply":{"description":"the message_id `ask` returned","type":"string"}},"required":["reply"],"type":"object"}]},"type":"array"}},"required":[],"type":"object"}},{"name":"send","description":"Send a message to a teammate, addressed by roster name, through the lead. With `reply_to`, it answers the question that identifier names, and the teammate waiting on that answer wakes. `scope` selects the team: the one this episode belongs to, or the one it leads, which is how a member answers a question its own child asked.","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"content":{"description":"the message","type":"string"},"reply_to":{"description":"the message_id of a question this answers","type":"string"},"scope":{"description":"member selects the team this episode belongs to, the default; led selects the team it leads","enum":["member","led"],"type":"string"},"to":{"description":"roster name of the teammate, or `lead` for the episode leading the team","type":"string"}},"required":["to","content"],"type":"object"}},{"name":"ask","description":"Ask a teammate a question, addressed by roster name, through the lead. It returns the question's `message_id`, and `wait` with `{reply: that id}` blocks until that question is answered and not until any message arrives. A question is bounded: `deadline_ms` says how long it stays open, `default` says what answer stands when that time passes with no answer, and the runtime delivers that answer itself, so no episode waits on another without end. `scope` selects the team: the one this episode belongs to, or the one it leads. Use it when one answer from one teammate decides what you do next; `send` is for telling.","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"content":{"description":"the question","type":"string"},"deadline_ms":{"description":"how long the question stays open, in milliseconds; when it passes with no answer the runtime delivers `default` as the answer","minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"default":{"description":"the answer that stands when the deadline passes with no answer","type":"string"},"scope":{"description":"member selects the team this episode belongs to, the default; led selects the team it leads","enum":["member","led"],"type":"string"},"to":{"description":"roster name of the teammate, or `lead` for the episode leading the team","type":"string"}},"required":["to","content","deadline_ms","default"],"type":"object"}},{"name":"notify","description":"Send a message to the episode that started this one.","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"content":{"description":"the message","type":"string"}},"required":["content"],"type":"object"}},{"name":"spawn","description":"Add a task to this episode's team. The runtime starts one child episode when its dependencies and the team budget permit. Returns the durable task state; the child's result arrives later as a message.","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"blocked_by":{"description":"task ids that must complete before this task starts","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"context":{"description":"fresh starts the child with only its task; fork seeds it with this episode's conversation so far","enum":["fresh","fork"],"type":"string"},"contract":{"description":"name of a contract listed in grants.spawn","type":"string"},"name":{"description":"roster name for the child; defaults to a unique form of the contract name","type":"string"},"task":{"description":"what the child is to do","type":"string"},"write":{"description":"the directories this worker may write in, each one that exists already, within your own and within what its contract allows, and not under or over a root another live task holds; naming a file, or a file the worker has yet to write, is refused; omitted, it writes nothing","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"}},"required":["contract","task"],"type":"object"}}],"model":{"provider":"host","model":"host"}}}
